{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>their heart</b> — You hear before they speak, after the manner of \"there is no word on my tongue\" [Psalm 139:4]. And all their desire — You prepare their heart, i.e., for their help. And the tav of תקשיב [You incline] is a sign of feminine language. And this meaning is doubled."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase וכל תאותם may be read as the continuation of the quoted verse allusion or as Ibn Ezra's own words; translated as his comment following the quotation mark."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:59.075206153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}